  "description": "The \u0027problem_connections\u0027 dataset is designed to track and analyze issues related to various connection attempts within a system. It includes detailed information about each connection, such as the name, type, and credentials mode, as well as the status and error messages associated with connection tests. This dataset is particularly useful for system administrators and developers who need to diagnose and resolve connectivity issues. It provides insights into common errors, such as insufficient quotas, and allows for the identification of patterns in connection failures. Additionally, the dataset includes metadata about who last modified the connection settings and whether write operations are allowed. This information can be crucial for auditing and compliance purposes. The dataset\u0027s structure, with fields for parameters like authentication type, scopes, and database details, makes it versatile for various use cases, including troubleshooting, performance monitoring, and system optimization. By analyzing this dataset, organizations can improve their connection reliability and user experience.",
  "shortDesc": "Dataset of connection issues with error messages and statuses.",
